[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
I tested end-to-end connectivity directly between the two reported hosts on the access switch. From PC15 (172.18.51.15) to PC16 (172.18.51.16) and back, ICMP pings succeed with 0% loss and sub‑3 ms RTTs. An iperf TCP test from PC15 to PC16 sustained ~100–120 Mbit/s with zero retransmissions, confirming reliable bidirectional L2/L3 and TCP data flow. Both endpoints’ NICs (eth0) are up with correct /24 addressing and a common default gateway (172.18.51.254), and no interface errors are present. This demonstrates that the L2 segment behind switch10 (ports cd_sw10_fa1_1 for PC15 and cd_sw10_fa2_1 for PC16) and the immediate access infrastructure are functioning normally.

Mechanism: If the switch port or VLAN were misconfigured, we would see ARP failures, ping loss, or TCP retransmissions; none are observed. Localization: The tested path is PC15 eth0 ↔ switch10 ↔ PC16 eth0; all elements behave correctly.

Root cause: No network-side fault found; the reported “cannot talk at all” condition is not reproducible—connectivity between PC15 and PC16 is currently normal.

Corrective fix: No changes needed on the network. If file sharing still fails at the users’ desks, verify application-layer services and host firewalls on PC15/PC16 (e.g., SMB/NFS service status and local firewall rules), since transport connectivity between the two hosts is confirmed healthy.
